We define theperturbation score 𝑝pertofΨ, denoted by 𝑝pertas
the probability thatΨsurvives a random perturbation trial:
𝑝pert=Pr[Ψsurvives a random perturbation trial].
In practice, 𝑝pertis estimated by the fraction of survivals over re-
peated trials. A low score indicates that Ψis sensitive to random
recombination and is therefore more likely to reflect a genuine re-
lationship, whereas a high score suggests Ψis spurious. We accept
Ψas stable only if𝑝 pert≤𝜂, where𝜂is a user-specified threshold.
