cost while preserving its discovery effectiveness.6 RELATED WORK
Dependency and Relationship Discovery.Functional dependen-
cies (FDs) and approximate functional dependencies (AFDs) have
been extensively studied in data profiling and data management.
Representative discovery algorithms (e.g., [ 3,31,49,67]) focus on ef-
ficiently enumerating minimalFDsfrom relational data, with a com-
prehensive experimental comparison provided by [ 52]. More recent
work continues to improveFDdiscovery, e.g., via hitting-set-based
enumeration [ 7], mixed-type extensions [ 47], and meaningfulness-
aware discovery [ 65], while relaxed and approximate variants have
11

